    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Chamorro language belongs to the Malayo-Polynesian subgroup of the Austronesian family and took many Spanish loanwords in more than 300 years of Spanish rule.</li><li>During the Japanese occupation of Guam from 1941 to 1944, Chamorros were subjected to forced labour, imprisonment, torture and execution.</li><li>Chamorro institutions on Guam advocate the spelling CHamoru, which the language commission announced as the preferred standard in 2018.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In the Chamorro creation story the dying Puntan had his sister Fu’una make the world from his body: his eyes became the Sun and Moon and his eyebrows the rainbows.</p></aside>
    </section>

